<Defs>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       THE DRAW TABLE

       Every archite gene in the active load order, hand-ranked. This is the
       one file to edit when the altar feels wrong.

       WHY BY HAND: the game's own numbers cannot separate these genes.
       biostatMet is 0 for all 50 but one, and biostatCpx is 3 for 35 of them
       - Deathless (cpx 7) and a cosmetic gene (cpx 3) look identical to any
       automatic rule. See docs/archite-gene-pool.md for the distribution.

       TIER - how much getting it changes the pawn:
         1  marginal
         2  solid, situational
         3  strong
         4  major
         5  campaign-defining
       The altar's outcome roll picks WHICH TIER BAND the four options are
       drawn from. It never decides whether you get something - a poor roll
       offers four weak genes, not nothing.

       RESERVED - never offered by the lottery at any tier or any roll.
       Reserved genes arrive only as named quest vectors, or never at all.

       CATEGORY - what the gene is for. Facilities linked to the altar bias
       the draw toward a category, which is what makes a war-altar draw
       differently from an artisan-altar.

       MayRequire guards every modded gene, so a removed mod drops that entry
       instead of throwing a cross-reference error on load.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <Archinity.GenePoolDef>
    <defName>Archinity_ArchitePool</defName>
    <entries>

      <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
           RESERVED: the founders' identity.

           Never in the pool, never a vector, never obtainable by anyone.
           Normal sanguophages already get Deathless and Ageless, so these
           alone do not make the founders unique - the Deathrest asymmetry
           does that. They are withheld anyway because the two originals
           should not be reachable by grinding the altar.
           --------------------------------------------------------------- -->
      <li>
        <gene>Deathless</gene>
        <tier>5</tier>
        <category>Survival</category>
        <reserved>true</reserved>
      </li>
      <li>
        <gene>Ageless</gene>
        <tier>4</tier>
        <category>Survival</category>
        <reserved>true</reserved>
      </li>

      <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
           RESERVED: chain milestones.

           Each of these is the payload of a specific quest beat, so letting
           the lottery hand one out early would defuse that beat.
           --------------------------------------------------------------- -->
